\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Computed the flat eight-dimensional product Green kernel and showed that multiplying four-dimensional Green functions gives the wrong source. All twistor, Einstein-limit, monopole and noncommutative harmonic-form questions remain unresolved.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied complete definition, catalogue wording, scope qualifications and source list for this canonical ID. The original-source citations are inherited as supplied references; no fresh primary-source or novelty search was performed for this attempt. No current open-status claim is inferred from this calculation.

\paragraph{A synchronized product Green kernel.}For the flat product \(\mathbb R^4_x\times\mathbb R^4_y\), the heat kernel is the product at the same time parameter,
\[H_t(x,y)=(4\pi t)^{-4}\exp[-(|x|^2+|y|^2)/(4t)].\]
Integrating from zero to infinity, with \(r^2=|x|^2+|y|^2>0\), gives
\[G_8(x,y)=\int_0^\infty H_t(x,y)dt=\frac1{2\pi^4r^6}.
\]
Indeed substitution \(s=r^2/(4t)\) reduces the integral to \((4\pi)^{-4}(4/r^2)^3\int_0^\infty s^2e^{-s}ds\), and the last integral is two by repeated integration by parts. Integrating the heat equation in time shows \(-\Delta G_8=\delta_0\) distributionally; the boundary at infinity vanishes and the small-time heat kernel converges to the delta distribution.
\paragraph{Why multiplying Green functions fails.}In four dimensions \(G_4(x)=1/(4\pi^2|x|^2)\). A product of two such Green functions satisfies
\[-\Delta_{x,y}[G_4(x)G_4(y)]=\delta_0(x)G_4(y)+G_4(x)\delta_0(y),\]
which has sources along the coordinate factors, rather than only at the product origin. Thus the product construction requires a synchronized heat integral, not the product of inverses.
\paragraph{Remaining full scope.}This is a flat eight-dimensional scalar-kernel benchmark. It does not extend Atiyah's Serre-class/twistor formalism or define its quaternionic analogue. Hyper-Kahler limits of quaternionic Einstein metrics, multi-monopole asymptotics, noncommutative instanton number, uniqueness of middle forms and the claimed n forms with circle holonomy all remain unproved. The first gap for the Green-function route is identifying a geometric cohomology construction compatible with the synchronized inverse and noncompact boundary conditions; the calculation alone provides no such correspondence.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked heat normalization, gamma integral, distributional Laplacian, coordinate-factor source and all bundled questions. This was an LLM adversarial audit, not independent human verification; no theorem prover was used. Prompts A then B applied to this ID: Checked heat normalization, gamma integral, distributional Laplacian, coordinate-factor source and all bundled questions. Scope remains limited: Construct the appropriate geometric/twistor cohomology correspondence for the eight-dimensional Green operator with controlled noncompact boundary behavior.

Coordinator checked the synchronized eight-dimensional heat integral and distributional sources of the incorrect product of Green functions. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

